{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall guard yourselves very much for your souls</b> — He warns them lest they stray after the voice that they heard, and commit corruption to hew down the plantings. He said first 'the form of male or female,' in man, for from them would come a voice, and afterward he mentioned everything that is on the earth among beasts and birds and creeping things of the ground and fish of the sea, and afterward he returned to the host of the heavens. I have already explained <b>which YHWH your Elohim has allotted to all the peoples</b> — that each of them has a star and constellation and celestial beings over them, angels of the Most High, as stated in Daniel: 'the prince of the kingdom of Persia' and 'the prince of the kingdom of Greece' (Daniel 10:20); and therefore they make themselves elohim from them and worship them. And he said: 'But you HaShem has taken' (Deuteronomy 4:20), for you are the portion of HaShem — you shall not establish over yourselves a prince or helper besides Him, for He brought you out of the iron furnace, that you were within Egypt in a furnace of fire and wood, and He brought you out from there against their princes whom He visited with plagues upon them; and had He not struck them down you would not have gone out, for they in their ascendancy intended that you should not go out. And behold, He did all this so that you would become an inheritance to Him and become for His great name a treasured people above all peoples."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:10.969646950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}